From 64185271c3b144ac5d8fc9bbee755d6ba3cafa40 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CufeHaco <redeagleteam2005@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:37:38 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] Move UNIX sockets to JEP-380 channels and FFM (#9040)

UNIXSocket, UNIXServer and Socket.new(:UNIX) now open the JDK's
unix-domain SocketChannel/ServerSocketChannel (JEP 380) instead of
jnr-unixsocket. What java.nio cannot do goes through FFM
(java.lang.foreign) downcalls in UnixDomainNative: socketpair(2) for
UNIXSocket.pair and Socket.socketpair (stream and datagram), raw
datagram sockets for Socket.new(:UNIX, :DGRAM), sendmsg/recvmsg with
SCM_RIGHTS for send_io/recv_io, getsockname/getpeername, fcntl and
poll. errno is captured with Linker.Option.captureCallState.

- UnixFdChannel wraps a raw fd (pair, for_fd, received fds, datagram
  sockets) and replaces jnr's fromFD.
- Named sockets read and write through UnixSocketNativeChannel: a plain
  blocking read(2)/write(2) on the real fd, as jnr did. The JDK
  channel's own read() closes the channel when the thread is
  interrupted, which broke Thread#raise/Timeout around reads.
- ChannelFD treats JEP-380 channels as native descriptors, so a
  blocking read skips the pre-read select.
- SocketType, FilenoUtil, PosixShim and the address helpers in
  BasicSocket/UNIXSocket/UNIXServer learn the new channel and address
  types; UnixDomainSocketAddress and jnr's UnixSocketAddress are both
  accepted.
- Fiber scheduler accept (master) runs on the new ServerSocketChannel.

Without --enable-native-access the FFM pieces fail closed: a stream pair falls
back to a temporary-path JEP-380 pair; datagram pairs and sockets need
native access.

Out of scope, carried here because the code above needs it: the
sendmsg_nonblock NotImplemented stub is replaced by waitFd (Ruby's
socket.rb defines sendmsg_nonblock in the next commit), and
Socket#connect's jnr branch goes with the EISCONN check that replaced it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
